{"strongs": "H0314", "word": "אַחֲרוֺן", "translit": "a.cha.ron", "root": "אחרון", "morph": "H:A", "pos": "feminine", "gloss": "from", "definition": "אַחֲרוֺן 51 feminine אַחֲרוֺנָה plural אַחֲרֹנִים (also אַחֲרוֺנִים adjective from אַחַר , coming after or behind (as a comparative or superlative, according to the context); hence \\ \\ a. of place, behind, hindermost Gen 33:2 (twice in verse); הָאַחֲרוֺן הַיָּם the hinder (= the Western) sea (i.e. the Mediterranean: opposed to הַיָּם הַקַּדְמוֺנִי the front sea = the Dead Sea, the Semites, in defining the quarters of the heavens, turning naturally to the East, compare קֶדֶם of the East, יָמִין , תֵּימָן of the South, above under the word אָחוֺר \\ \\ d. and Assyrian mat a—arru 'the Western land,' of Phoenicia & Palestine) Deut 11:24 ; Deut 34:2 ; Joel 2:20 ; Zech 14:8 ; Job 18:20 poetic אַחֲרֹנִים Ew Hi Di De the dwellers in the West (opposed to קַדְמוֺנִים ). More commonly \\ \\ b. of time, latter or last (according to context) Exod 4:8 ; Deut 24:3 ; 2Sam 19:12 ; Isa 8:23 , of God Isa 44:6 (|| רִאשׁוֺן ) Isa 48:12 (do.) compare Isa 41:4 in genl. subsequent (vaguely), ׳ יוֺם א = time to come Isa 30:8 ; Prov 31:25 (but Neh 8:18 הַיוֺם ׳ הָאַ = the last day), ׳ (הָ)אַ (הַ)דּוֺר the following generation Deut 29:21 ; Ps 48:14 ; Ps 78:4 ; Ps 78:6 ; Ps 102:19 , (הָ)אַחֲרֹנִים they that come after Job 18:20 ( Ges Schl ) Eccl 1:11 ; Eccl 4:16 , but Isa 41:4 the last , Job 19:25 וְאַחֲרוֺן עַלעָֿפָר יָקוּם and as one coming after (me) (and so able to establish my innocence when I am dead) will he ( גָֹּֽאֲלִי my Vindicator) arise upon the dust. — The feminine is used adverbially (compare רִאשֹׁנָה ) = afterwards or at the last (according to context): \\ \\ \\ ( a ) absolute Dan 11:29 ( β ) בָּאַחֲרוֺנָה (opposed to בָּרִאשֹׁנָה ) Deut 13:10 ; Deut 17:7 ; Deut 1:2 ; Deut 2:26 ; Deut 1:13 ; ( γ ) ׳ לָאַ Num 2:31 ( P ) Eccl 1:11 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB341')\">BDB341</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H314')\">H314</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB340')\">BDB340</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB342')\">BDB342</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אַחֲרוֺן</bdbheb><sub>51</sub> <b>feminine</b> <bdbheb>אַחֲרוֺנָה</bdbheb> plural <bdbheb>אַחֲרֹנִים</bdbheb> (also <bdbheb>אַחֲרוֺנִים</bdbheb> <b>adjective</b> <highlightword>from</highlightword> <bdbheb>אַחַר</bdbheb>, coming after or behind (as a comparative or superlative, according to the context); hence <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> of place, <highlight>behind, hindermost</highlight> <ref ref=\"Gen 33:2\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(1,33,2)\">Gen 33:2</ref> (twice in verse); <bdbheb>הָאַחֲרוֺן הַיָּם</bdbheb> <highlight>the hinder</highlight> (= the Western) sea (i.e. the Mediterranean: opposed to <bdbheb>הַיָּם הַקַּדְמוֺנִי</bdbheb> the front sea = the Dead Sea, the Semites, in defining the quarters of the heavens, turning naturally to the East, compare <bdbheb>קֶדֶם</bdbheb> of the East, <bdbheb>יָמִין</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>תֵּימָן</bdbheb> of the South, above under the word <bdbheb>אָחוֺר</bdbheb> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> and Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>mat a—arru</highlight></transliteration> 'the Western land,' of Phoenicia &amp; Palestine) <ref ref=\"Deut 11:24\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(5,11,24)\">Deut 11:24</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 34:2\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(5,34,2)\">Deut 34:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Joel 2:20\" b=\"29\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(29,2,20)\">Joel 2:20</ref>; <ref ref=\"Zech 14:8\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(38,14,8)\">Zech 14:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 18:20\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(18,18,20)\">Job 18:20</ref> poetic <bdbheb>אַחֲרֹנִים</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hi')\">Hi</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup> <highlight>the dwellers in the West</highlight> (opposed to <bdbheb>קַדְמוֺנִים</bdbheb>). More commonly <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> of time, <highlight>latter</highlight> or <highlight>last</highlight> (according to context) <ref ref=\"Exod 4:8\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(2,4,8)\">Exod 4:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 24:3\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(5,24,3)\">Deut 24:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 19:12\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(10,19,12)\">2Sam 19:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 8:23\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(23,8,23)\">Isa 8:23</ref>, of God <ref ref=\"Isa 44:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,6)\">Isa 44:6</ref> (|| <bdbheb>רִאשׁוֺן</bdbheb>) <ref ref=\"Isa 48:12\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(23,48,12)\">Isa 48:12</ref> (do.) compare <ref ref=\"Isa 41:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,41,4)\">Isa 41:4</ref> in genl. <highlight>subsequent</highlight> (vaguely), <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>יוֺם א</bdbheb> = time <highlight>to come</highlight> <ref ref=\"Isa 30:8\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(23,30,8)\">Isa 30:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 31:25\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(20,31,25)\">Prov 31:25</ref> (but <ref ref=\"Neh 8:18\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(16,8,18)\">Neh 8:18</ref> <bdbheb>הַיוֺם</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הָאַ</bdbheb> = <highlight>the last</highlight> day), <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>(הָ)אַ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>(הַ)דּוֺר</bdbheb> <highlight>the following</hi